====================================================================================================
3. mapping physical helicities to spin projections on a common axis (B&O's eq. 6 labels)
====================================================================================================
Head-on CM: J along +z of the graviton pair = l1 - l2 (graviton 2 moves along -z).
Photon pair along n: J along n = s1 - s2.  Nonzero physical configurations found above:
  physical (l1,l2,s1,s2) = (2, -2, 1, -1):  J_z(gg) = +4, J_n(gamma gamma) = +2;  |M|/(8 pi G) = u^2/s;  common-axis label (g-axis k1, photon axis q1): A_++++;  (g-axis k1, photon axis q2): A_++--
  physical (l1,l2,s1,s2) = (2, -2, -1, 1):  J_z(gg) = +4, J_n(gamma gamma) = -2;  |M|/(8 pi G) = t^2/s;  common-axis label (g-axis k1, photon axis q1): A_++--;  (g-axis k1, photon axis q2): A_++++
  physical (l1,l2,s1,s2) = (-2, 2, 1, -1):  J_z(gg) = -4, J_n(gamma gamma) = +2;  |M|/(8 pi G) = t^2/s;  common-axis label (g-axis k1, photon axis q1): A_--++;  (g-axis k1, photon axis q2): A_----
  physical (l1,l2,s1,s2) = (-2, 2, -1, 1):  J_z(gg) = -4, J_n(gamma gamma) = -2;  |M|/(8 pi G) = u^2/s;  common-axis label (g-axis k1, photon axis q1): A_----;  (g-axis k1, photon axis q2): A_--++
B&O eq. 6: A++++ = A---- = 8 pi G t^2/s,  A++-- = A--++ = 8 pi G u^2/s, others zero.
Physical-helicity reading of B&O's labels: A++++ would be (l1,l2,s1,s2) = (2,2,1,1): module |M| = 2.1e-14 (zero) -> that reading is refuted.
Common-axis reading: magnitudes and zeros match; with the graviton axis along k1 and the photon axis along q2
(or along k2 and q1) the t/u assignment is exactly B&O's; with axes (k1, q1) t and u are interchanged,
which only relabels the two photons and cannot change any integrated rate.

====================================================================================================
4. rephasing-invariant phases: can all eq.-6 amplitudes be made real & positive by a choice of conventions?
====================================================================================================
For fixed photons (q1, q2) and two graviton axes a, a' on the ring k1 + k2 = q1 + q2 (same K), the product
  I(a, a') = M_a(+2,-2 -> +1,-1) M_a(+2,-2 -> -1,+1)^* M_a'(+2,-2 -> -1,+1) M_a'(+2,-2 -> +1,-1)^*
is invariant under every rephasing of graviton and photon helicity states. Eq. 6 as real positive numbers
would force arg I = 0 for all a, a'.
  photons at theta=60, phi=17:  arg I(a=0, a') for a' tilted by 30 deg:   +63.87, 60 deg:   -17.09, 90 deg:  -125.78
  photons at theta=60, phi=45:  arg I(a=0, a') for a' tilted by 30 deg:  +126.66, 60 deg:   -46.80, 90 deg:  +106.26
  photons at theta=100, phi=10:  arg I(a=0, a') for a' tilted by 30 deg:   +21.15, 60 deg:   +52.85, 90 deg:  -178.25
=> nonzero rephasing-invariant phases: no phase convention makes all eq.-6 amplitudes real and positive at once;
   eq. 6 is correct for the MAGNITUDES only, and a coherent sum over different graviton pairs (eq. 7) needs the
   phases.
